  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the woman via the pronoun 'me' in the text",
  "description": "The text 'i support terrorists because they're pea brains like me' explicitly uses the first-person pronoun 'me', which directly maps the speaker (the woman in the visual material) onto the user's perspective. The user is projected onto the woman as the subject of the self-referential statement, creating an identification where the user sees themselves as the 'me' referenced in the hateful text. This projection is explicit and direct, using the deictic pronoun 'me' to anchor the user's identity onto the visual subject.",
